This license (LGPL v3) applies to all parts of kRPC except for the following:

  - protobuf/* is under the MIT license.

  - service/SpaceCenter/* is under the GPLv3 license.

  - service/Debug/* is under the GPLv3 license.

  - service/InfernalRobotics/* is under the GPLv3 license.

  - tools/krpctools/* is under the GPLv3 license.

  - tools/ServiceDefinitions/* is under the GPLv3 license.

  - experimental/ksa/release/ holds the license files of the kRPC for KSA release,
    which cover the third-party binaries it ships.

  - As an additional permission under section 7 of the GNU GPL v3, code that krpctools
    generates for a client, including the service stubs shipped with each client and
    their documentation, is under the license of that client, whatever the license of
    krpctools or of the service it is generated from.

Why the parts are licensed this way:

  - The server, core and clients are under the LGPL. Any program can use the
    clients, including closed source and commercial ones, and changes to kRPC itself
    stay open. Scripts talk to the server over a connection, so the server's license
    does not extend to them.

  - The protocol schema is under the MIT license, so that anyone can implement a client
    for it under any license.

  - The SpaceCenter, Debug and InfernalRobotics services contain code adapted from
    GPLv3 mods, listed below, so they are under the GPLv3.

  - krpctools and ServiceDefinitions are under the GPLv3 for historical reasons.

Code adapted from other projects:

  - service/SpaceCenter/src/Services/CelestialBody.cs: the surface raycast is adapted
    from kOS (https://github.com/KSP-KOS/KOS), released under the GPLv3.

  - service/SpaceCenter/src/Services/SpaceCenter.cs: the time warp control is adapted
    from MechJeb2 (https://github.com/MuMech/MechJeb2), released under the GPLv3.

  - service/SpaceCenter/src/ExtensionMethods/StockAerodynamics.cs is adapted from
    the KSP Trajectories mod (https://github.com/neuoy/KSPTrajectories), released
    under the MIT License (MIT) by Youen Toupin, aka neuoy

  - service/Debug/src/Debug.cs: the landing velocity damping is from HyperEdit
    (https://github.com/Ezriilc/HyperEdit), released under the GPLv3.

  - service/InfernalRobotics/src/IRWrapper.cs is adapted from Infernal Robotics
    (https://github.com/MagicSmokeIndustries/InfernalRobotics), released under the GPLv3.

  - service/KerbalAlarmClock/src/KACWrapper.cs is from Kerbal Alarm Clock
    (https://github.com/TriggerAu/KerbalAlarmClock), released under the MIT License (MIT)
    by David Tregoning

  - client/python/krpc/decoder.py contains code from Google's protobuf project.
    See tools/build/protobuf/LICENSE.Google.Protobuf

  - tools/TestingTools/src/AutoLoadGame.cs and AutoSwitchVessel.cs are adapted
    from the AutoLoadGame plugin, released under the MIT License (MIT) by Allis Tauri

